 "text": "Hi! How's everything today? A sketch is a quick drawing, usually done without much thought, and a study is a formal detailed drawing. Kind of. Studies often involve lot of research, looking at real things in libraries or online, and drawing them. For that, a sketchbook is where you start. Look at real pictures of clouds, and sketch them from life. Then your drawing of the clouds in your painting will be more believable. Light, shapes, and how things fade into each other, not details. A quick, loose line is fine. That's the spirit.",
